      <h2 id="buying-guide">How to Choose a ChatGPT Alternative in 2026</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Step 1 — Identify your primary task:</strong> Writing and reasoning → Claude. Google ecosystem → Gemini. Coding → Copilot. Research with citations → Perplexity. Real-time social data → Grok.</li>
        <li><strong>Step 2 — Start free:</strong> Claude, Gemini, Copilot, and Perplexity all have free tiers. Use each for one real task before paying.</li>
        <li><strong>Step 3 — Evaluate context window:</strong> If you process long documents (100K+ words), Claude (200K) and Gemini 1.5 Pro (1M) are the leaders.</li>
        <li><strong>Step 4 — Check ecosystem integration:</strong> Google users get Gemini integration for free. Developers get Copilot in their IDE. Researchers get Perplexity's cited search.</li>
        <li><strong>Step 5 — Consider stacking:</strong> Many power users pay for two tools — e.g., Claude Pro for writing + Copilot for coding, or Perplexity Pro for research + Gemini for Google integration.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>Learn more about our <a href="/how-we-test/">testing methodology</a> and <a href="/editorial-policy/">editorial policy</a>.</p>

