      <div class="faq">
        <details>
          <summary>What is the best free alternative to ChatGPT in 2026?</summary>
          <p>Claude (free tier) and Google Gemini (free tier) are the best free ChatGPT alternatives. Claude's free tier offers strong writing quality and a 200K context window. Gemini free includes multimodal capabilities (image, voice, and video understanding) with Google Search integration. For research with citations, Perplexity Free offers 5 Pro searches per day.</p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>Is Claude better than ChatGPT?</summary>
          <p>Claude is better than ChatGPT for long-form writing, nuanced reasoning, and processing large documents (200K context window vs GPT-4o's 128K). ChatGPT is better for coding assistance (with Copilot integration), multimodal tasks, and custom GPTs. For most writing and analysis tasks, Claude produces more natural prose. For coding and app-like workflows, ChatGPT with GPTs wins.</p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>Which AI is best for coding besides ChatGPT?</summary>
          <p>GitHub Copilot is the best AI for coding in an IDE (VS Code, JetBrains) because it integrates directly into the editor with autocomplete and inline suggestions. Claude (via the Claude web interface or API) is best for code review and architecture discussions because of its large context window. For pair-programming with a chat interface, Cursor (built on VS Code) is a strong dedicated coding AI.</p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>Is Perplexity better than ChatGPT for research?</summary>
          <p>Perplexity is better than ChatGPT for research that requires current sources and citations. Perplexity searches the web in real-time and cites every claim with source links, making it ideal for fact-checking and literature review. ChatGPT (with web search enabled) is comparable but less citation-focused. For academic or journalistic research, Perplexity Pro at $20/month is the stronger research tool.</p>
